37
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:52.534
Tadpole, Tadpole, Tadpole! Lily pad, Lily pad! Swan, Swan, Swan! Goose, Goose, Goose!

38
00:01:52.584 --> 00:02:00.461
Reed, Reed, Reed! Pebble, Pebble, Pebble! Newt, Newt, Newt! Ripple, Ripple, Ripple!

39
00:02:00.511 --> 00:02:03.653
Clap, clap! Great chanting!

40
00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:14.331
At the pond, a tadpole swims under a lily pad. A white swan glides by. I throw a pebble and see a ripple in the water.

41
00:02:14.381 --> 00:02:17.213
I love this story, Ms. Lily!

42
00:02:18.116 --> 00:02:23.702
What is it? Can you say it?

43
00:02:23.752 --> 00:02:26.040
Ripple! Well done!

44
00:02:27.016 --> 00:02:32.497
What is it? Can you say it?

45
00:02:32.547 --> 00:02:34.850
Pebble! Well done!

46
00:02:35.949 --> 00:02:41.640
What is it? Can you say it?

47
00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.127
Swan! Well done!

48
00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:47.225
Let's say it together!

49
00:02:47.275 --> 00:02:52.006
The tadpole lives in the pond. The swan lives in the pond.

50
00:02:52.056 --> 00:02:56.571
Your turn!

51
00:02:56.621 --> 00:03:01.157
The tadpole lives in the pond. The swan lives in the pond.

52
00:03:02.142 --> 00:03:07.110
What lives in a pond?

53
00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.568
The tadpole lives in the pond.

54
00:03:09.618 --> 00:03:10.935
Great answer!

55
00:03:11.935 --> 00:03:16.651
Today's value is patience. Wait quietly and watch.

56
